    "long_instructions": "# Predict & Run\r\n\r\nLook at the code in the workspace. The Painter starts at the left end of the street, facing east. A taxi is parked at the far end.\r\n\r\nPredict what will happen: How many times will \"I moved!\" print, and where will the Painter end up?\r\n\r\nWrite your prediction.\r\n\r\nPress Run to check your answer.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from neighborhood import *\n\n# Painter setup: the Painter starts at the left end of the street, facing east.\nmove()\nmove()\nmove()\nmove()\n\n# Check 1\nif can_move():\n    move()\n    print(\"I moved!\")\n\n# Check 2\nif can_move():\n    move()\n    print(\"I moved!\")",
          "folderId": "0",
