    "teacher_markdown": "What students predict and what happens:\r\n\r\n- The program prints \"I moved!\" once, and the Painter ends one square before the taxi.\r\n- Most students predict two prints and two moves, because the same check appears twice. The second check asks the same question, but the answer has changed.\r\n- After the setup, the Painter is at the second-to-last square. Check 1 is True, so it moves and prints. Check 2 asks again, and now the taxi is ahead, so the condition is False and the block is skipped.\r\n- Skipped code is not an error. Nothing prints for Check 2, and the program ends normally.\r\n- The Painter walks over the bucket during the setup and does not take paint, because nothing asks it to.\r\n- Do not explain the result before students run the program. The Investigate level that follows uses this program."
  },
